//Most of these are from The Faces of Evil.
QUIT1 =		"Oh come on, elves can't be THAT bad.";
QUIT2 =		"My boy, these guns are what ALL true warriors strive for!";
QUIT3 =		"See how D'Sparil makes HIS warriors!";
QUIT4 =		"At last, you have the vision to find my house!";
QUIT5 =		"Oh goodie; Mashed Corvus for the main course!";
QUIT6 =		"Hey! Wanna fight the forces of evil in Korodai?";
QUIT7 =		"Join me, Corvus, and I will make your face the greatest in "
			"Pathorsis, or else you will die!";
QUIT8 =		"Such is the power of D'sparil that he can kill with a single look!";
QUIT9 =		"Consider Lupay, the most dangerous of D'Sparil's minions.";
QUIT10 =	"You defeat D'sparil by throwing a book, now get on the fucking "
			"carpet!"; //iTeachVader - Alternate Endings
QUIT11 =	"A whole month gone, and still no word.";
QUIT12 =	"And the last word he spoke, as his head rolled across the floor "
			"was...\n\n\"'WAAAAAAAAAAAAARGH!!!\""; //Insomniac Ren
QUIT13 =	"I saw a mudcrab the other day, filthy things."; //Skyrim
QUIT14 =	"Sorry, no funny quit message here.\nThey can't all be winners.";
QUIT15 =	"Enabling Sparklies lets you acess even more modes of firing, just "
			"in case the weapons weren't overpowered enough!";
QUIT16 =	"Your melee waepons don't have any special attacking modes. Sorry.";
QUIT17 =	"If thou'st need to take thy olde dump, firste ditch'eth the "
			"terrib'leth butcher'ed olde English'e.";
QUIT18 =	"Guns don't kill people, wands do!\n"
			"Yeah, old joke, but who's keeping track.";
QUIT19 =	"n o r d    m e a d"; //Skyrim Fansong
QUIT20 =	"Stuffing 150+ functions in a base class is not a good idea.";
QUIT21 =	"If you're familiar with how the fists work in Marathon, "
			"you'll probably find the staff to be useful in a pinch.";
QUIT22 =	"...what? Were you expecting a certain dragon?"; //Guncaster (or: a better mod)
QUIT23 =	"Too much magic!\nTOO MUCH MAGIC!!!"; //Scoot - TF2
QUIT24 =	"\"E!? YOU SOUND JUST LIKE MINI-ME FROM AUSTIN POWERS!\""; //TearOfGrace - Gollum
QUIT25 =	"It's nice to see Vasali again."; //I've missed you, VLIF.

